# ALLINONE-AGENT — per-agent Paperclip profile env (EXAMPLE)
#
# This is the REAL per-agent configuration surface documented in
# docs/legacy-platform-docs/PAPERCLIP-INTEGRATION.md: each Hermes worker profile
# (profiles\pc<role>\.env under ALLINONE_HERMES_HOME) gets its own scoped Paperclip API key,
# kept separate from the platform-wide config\platform.local.env.
#
# This is NOT a single monolithic "paperclip.json" — no such file exists in the reference
# implementation. Paperclip itself (the upstream app) is a pinned-reference dependency (see
# upstream/components.lock.json), not vendored into this repo, and has its own configuration
# docs (paperclip/doc/instance-configuration.md, agent-configuration-yaml.md) — refer to those
# for Paperclip's own settings rather than duplicating them here.
#
# Copy this to profiles\pc<role>\.env for EACH agent role, with a key scoped to that specific
# agent (requested via POST /api/agents/:id/keys against your own Paperclip instance — never
# share one key across all 11 agent profiles).

PAPERCLIP_API_KEY=
PAPERCLIP_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3100
PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID=
PAPERCLIP_TASK_ID=
PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID=
PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID=
